\ exp/165-no-cstack/nocstack.ff
\ Prove that x64 flow control can use mrk-chain instead of >cs/cs>
\
\ Strategy: redefine flow control as x-prefixed words using the
\ longconds/i386 mrk-chain technique for BREAK resolution.
\
\ The mrk layout (2 cells, same as ff2.boot):
\   mrk[0]: loop body address (backward jump target)
\   mrk[8]: break chain head (address of last BREAK's d, field, or 0)
\
\ BREAK chain: each BREAK emits E9 + 4-byte d, field. That field
\ holds the address of the previous BREAK's d, field (or 0 sentinel).
\ END walks the chain, patching each with the correct forward offset.
\
\ Old mrk values are saved/restored on the compile-time data stack
\ (the regular Forth stack during compilation), same as i386.

\ _then for long jumps: patch 4-byte rel32 at addr
:. x_then here over- 4- swap d! 0 callmark! ;

\ save/restore mrk on compile-time stack
:. x_begin mrk 2@ here mrk! 0 mrk 8+ ! ;

\ backward jumps
:. x_jmpback >S0 $E9 c, mrk@ here 4+ - d, ;
:. x_cjmpback >S0 cond $0F c, $10+ c, mrk@ here 4+ - d, ;

\ resolve break chain: ( chain_head -- ) walk linked list
:. x_resolve_breaks 0; dup d@ swap x_then x_resolve_breaks ;

\ resolve WHILE forward refs on compile-time stack (0 = sentinel from BEGIN)
:. x_resolve_fwds 0- 0> IF THEN` x_resolve_fwds THEN ;

\ restore mrk from compile-time stack (pushed by x_begin)
\ stack at this point: ( old_mrk0 old_mrk8 sentinel 0_or_whiles... )
\ x_resolve_fwds already consumed WHILEs, leaving sentinel (0 or -1)
\ Leave sentinel on stack for REPEAT to check (RTIMES uses -1)
:. x_end mrk 8+ @ x_resolve_breaks >r mrk 2! r> ;

\ --- public flow control words ---
: xBEGIN` >S0 x_begin 0 ;
: xSTART` x_begin 0 $E9 c, 0 d, here mrk! ;
: xTIMES` >r`
: xRTIMES` >S0 x_begin -1 $240CFF48, ,4 $880F, ,2 here 4 allot ;
: xENTER` >S0 mrk@ 4- x_then ;
: xWHILE.` cond.
: xWHILE` IF` ;
: xBREAK` >S0 $E9 c, mrk 8+ @ d, here 4- mrk 8+ ! THEN` ;
: xTILL.` cond.
: xTILL` >S0 cond $0F c, $10+ c, mrk@ here 4+ - d, ;
: xAGAIN` x_jmpback 0- 0<> IF THEN` ELSE x_end drop THEN ;
: xUNTIL.` cond.
: xUNTIL` x_cjmpback x_resolve_fwds x_end drop ;
: xEND` >S0 x_resolve_fwds x_end drop ;
: xREPEAT` x_jmpback x_resolve_fwds x_end 0- 0<> drop IF rdrop` THEN ;
